since we can't travel in person we  created share your world  a show where fellow travel lovers and i  share experiences from our cultural  backgrounds  in this episode we're saving room for  desserts  some save it for the end of the meal and  others skip straight to it  no matter how you enjoy them desserts  are a sweet form of comfort food served  around the world  my favorite armenian dessert is gata  it's like a sweet round  pastry and it's just really good when  you have it with like tea  or in the morning as breakfast or just a  pastry on its own  also with gata sometimes the bakers put  a little coin  in there and whoever gets like the slice  with the coin is set to have  good luck so i remember as a kid i would  always like eat so much just  so i can get the coin and i can get the  good luck if you go  to like villages like gagne and gerard  those women  over there make it a certain way and  they usually put like armenian letters  over it  um or they write gerard which is the  place that they are from  so one of my favorite cambodian desserts  is sticky rice with mango and coconut  milk  i actually went to cambodia and my uncle  owns a restaurant  where he actually made the dessert for  me so the mango is not your typical  mango  it's this long yellow mango as opposed  to the green and red one  and it's more like overly shaped than  the round circle  when you eat foods that have emotional  connections to it i think it does taste  better  so every time i eat it now again i  i remember of my time in cambodia  so whenever i visit korea the first  thing i do  is i go get this dessert called popping  zoo it's a shaved ice it's about  die high they put condensed milk they  put fruit pieces they put mochi rice  cakes red bean and you can get like  matcha flavor vanilla hazelnut  it's so refreshing and much much lighter  than ice cream  so the last time i went to visit my  parents i stayed at the jw marriott  hotel in seoul  and it's in this neighborhood called  myeongdong and they just have  all these street vendors late at night  and like a ton of food options and  there's a ton of shopping in the area  so i will drag my parents out at like 11  midnight  and we will go stop by all the little  street vendors and then  for like a dessert drink there's this  sweet rice milk  it's not thick at all so it's like the  consistency of lemonade  and it's slightly sweet and it's  refreshing and has little pieces of rice  in it so then you kind of like at the  end you kind of like swirl it so you can  get all the rice chunks even though i  like to buy the sweet rice drink i  always want my mom to make a whole batch  as well  so i'll use my marriott bomboy boundless  card to earn points by buying all the  ingredients  so it's so beneficial because i'm like  spending it on the car but also earning  points so i just feel like it all works  out great  having this card i will travel anywhere  just to try all the best desserts  the best snacks the best meals like i'm  all about it you know to me  food is also art i'm with you on that  plus one on the foodie i will travel for  food as well  yep honestly when i was younger my  biggest dream was working in a swiss  bakery  because i just love every bit of pastry  that we have back home  and when you go to swiss bakery the way  they present it  it's just absolutely beautiful two of my  favorite pastries which  i mean you have it here in america as  well it's carrot cake and a black forest  cake  we can buy it here in america but it's  just obviously not the same recipe  it's different back home so the  chocolate that's on top of the black  forest cake in switzerland  it's just this very thinly sliced  chocolate  and inside the black forest cake there's  dark cherries and i think here in  america a lot of times it's the bright  red cherries  they're just softer and they have a much  richer taste to it the carrot cake back  home is really just  uh the cake base with carrots in it and  then the top  is uh like a sugary glaze uh that you  make yourself you can add some lemon to  it for flavor  and then we actually have little um  carrot shaped marzipans  that we like decorate it with i  literally can't get enough of it so  whenever i go to switzerland  you bet i'm gonna eat those things  [Laughter]  yeah like with switzerland you know  you're gonna try chocolate but  like no one told me i should try the  carrot cake too  yeah cause it's i said like because we  like in america you know carrot cakes  it's not something  that you would necessarily try in a  different country because it's not  specific to switzerland  it's just the way that we make it is  different we're surrounded by a bunch of  countries it is germany just for  instance italy  it's a very small country but very very  international  so we do like to borrow ideas and  recipes  from our surrounding countries i am  so hungry after our conversation i  definitely learned a lot and i can't  wait to try  everything that we talked about if you  got a sweet tooth from watching this  video  we hope you're inspired to start  planning your next dessert-filled  [Music]  adventure  [Music]  you
 

